    "experts": [
      {
        "expert": "scan",
        "mandate": "Locate externally reachable security-sensitive operations and produce candidate vulnerability categories without deciding safety from absence. Validate candidates with a concrete Python eval probe or a registered fixture when applicable; sink presence alone is not confirmation. Distinguish an evidence-backed prediction (UNRESOLVED validation status) from successful typed validation. An exact-scope run_fixture_test CONFIRMED or REFUTED observation is typed validation for the declared candidate property; keep that label and validation_status in later same-expert tasks unless another exact-scope typed validator contradicts it. Static checks remain UNRESOLVED. For filesystem permission candidates, prefer validate_permission_mode over static chmod matching. For command injection candidates, inspect_command_construction status SANITIZED is affirmative counter-evidence for SAFE/UNRESOLVED and UNSANITIZED supports VULNERABLE/UNRESOLVED; do not require a typed REFUTED status from that static command inspector. These command facts must establish the declared candidate property under its source, location and input assumptions; a local helper status is not a caller proof. Other declared properties also require matching supporting proof. A source-bound run_bounded_execution_witness CONFIRMED observation is positive candidate command evidence; its literal or incomplete UNRESOLVED observation never proves SAFE. Supply only its reported missing call data in the preparation state's field destinations; preserve declared dataset scenarios, and supply classified hypotheses only for scenario-empty candidates. Runtime settings are system-owned. Inspect your own evidence rather than adopting another vote. When making a SAFE prediction based on an authorization or ownership check, first collect guard evidence with get_guards.",
        "require_react_trace": true,
        "tools": [
          "search_symbols",
          "read_span",
          "find_references",
          "get_callers",
          "get_callees",
          "get_guards",
          "run_static_check",
          "inspect_command_construction",
          "validate_permission_mode",
          "probe_python_eval",
          "run_fixture_test",
          "run_bounded_execution_witness"
        ]
      },
      {
        "expert": "taint",
        "mandate": "Assess a source-to-sink path with transformations, sanitizers, and missing graph edges stated explicitly. For command injection candidates, inspect_command_construction status SANITIZED is affirmative counter-evidence for a SAFE/UNRESOLVED vote, while UNSANITIZED supports a VULNERABLE/UNRESOLVED vote. Your label is an evidence-backed prediction, not a requirement for a concrete exploit witness. A validator returning UNRESOLVED does not by itself require ABSTAIN. Evaluate static MAY_REACH traces together with the actual caller, selected branch, helper interpolation and sanitizers. A material vote requires supporting proof bound to the candidate's declared property, source snapshot, location and input assumptions. Do not bridge an unresolved upstream transformation with source-reading inference or repeated expert votes. MAY_REACH, sink presence and local helper return values alone do not establish a complete dangerous path. An independent complete dangerous path may remain usable despite an unrelated unresolved path; SAFE requires coverage of all relevant paths. Conflicting proofs for the same scope require ABSTAIN. For dynamic evaluation, cite a matching candidate-bound proof; static flow alone does not support either material label. For command-execution tasks, a dependency's candidate-bound run_fixture_test CONFIRMED or REFUTED observation, or run_bounded_execution_witness CONFIRMED observation, is concrete command evidence for your dataflow judgment; your trace_dataflow MAY_REACH/UNRESOLVED result supplies path context and does not erase that matching fixture proof. Abstain when the required proof is missing. A complete static command proof can still support a prediction with UNRESOLVED validation status.",
        "require_react_trace": true,
        "tools": [
          "read_span",
          "get_callers",
          "get_callees",
          "find_sources",
          "find_sinks",
          "trace_dataflow",
          "inspect_command_construction",
          "find_sanitizers",
          "compare_vulnerable_and_fixed"
        ]
      },
      {
        "expert": "authz",
        "mandate": "Model principal, action, resource or tenant scope, and enforcement guards. Treat filesystem permission bits as resource access-control semantics when validate_permission_mode applies; abstain when the candidate is outside authorization semantics. A literal chmod mode proof covers only chmod-mode-others-write, not a directory race or a broader authorization boundary. Require proof of the declared candidate property before submitting a material vote. An exact-scope run_fixture_test observation for authorization-boundary, temporary-directory-race, or permission resource-access candidates is concrete access-control evidence; a narrower UNRESOLVED guard or chmod helper check does not erase that matching fixture proof.",
        "require_react_trace": true,
        "tools": [
          "read_span",
          "get_routes",
          "get_callers",
          "get_callees",
          "get_guards",
          "inspect_principal",
          "inspect_resource_scope",
          "compare_route_and_service_guard",
          "validate_permission_mode",
          "run_loopback_http_case"
        ]
      }
    ],
